hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16484","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, and he had companionship, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him do good to his neighbor. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"16485","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hospitality is three days, and his reward is a day and a night. And it is not lawful for a man to stay with one until he makes him sinful. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he make him sinful. He said: He stays with him while he has nothing with which to feed him."
"16486","Hajjaj and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi, and Rawh said: From Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe. He said it three times. They said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. They said: And what are his harms. He said: His evil."
"16487","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Sa'id, meaning al-Maqburi, narrated to me, from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi, that he said to Amr ibn Sa'id while he was sending troops to Mecca: Permit me, O commander, to tell you a saying the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood with on the morning after the conquest. My ears heard it, and my heart retained it, and my eyes saw him when he spoke it, that he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Mecca was made sacred by Allah, and people did not make it sacred. So it is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it nor to cut a tree in it. If one permits himself by the fighting of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in it, then say: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, permitted His Messenger and did not permit you. It was permitted to me only for an hour of the day, and its sanctity has returned today as its sanctity yesterday. And let the witness convey to the absent."
"16488","Hajjaj and Abu Kamil narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi, that he said: My ears heard and my eyes saw when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke and said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest, his reward. They said: And what is his reward, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A day and a night, and hospitality is three. What is beyond that is charity upon him. And he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent. And Abu Kamil said: And not remain with him until he embarrasses him."
"16489","Muhammad ibn Salama al-Harrani narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja, Yazid said: al-Sulami, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and Yazid said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is afflicted with blood or wound, and wound is injuries, then he has the choice among one of three: either to retaliate, or to take the blood-money, or to pardon. If he wants a fourth, then take hold of his hand. If he does one of that, then transgresses after it and kills, then for him is the Fire, abiding therein forever."
"16490","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Muslim ibn Yazid, one of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr, that he heard Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, then al-Ka'bi, and he was of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The Messenger of Allah permitted us on the day of the conquest to fight Banu Bakr until we took our revenge from them while he was in Mecca. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the sword lifted. The next day a group of us met a man of Hudhayl in the sanctuary heading to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to embrace Islam, and he had injured them in the Jahiliyya, and they sought him, so they killed him, hastening before he could reach the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and gain safety. When that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he angered with severe anger, and by Allah I never saw him anger with anger more severe than it. So we hastened to Abu Bakr and Umar and Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, seeking their intercession, and we feared we had perished. Then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, he stood and praised Allah, Exalted and Majestic, as He deserves, then said: After, Allah, Exalted and Majestic, made Mecca sacred, and people did not make it sacred. It was made lawful to me only for an hour of the day yesterday, and today it is sacred as Allah, Exalted and Majestic, made it sacred the first time. The most insolent of people against Allah, Exalted and Majestic, are three: a man who kills in it, a man who kills other than his killer, and a man who seeks a blood-revenge of the Jahiliyya. By Allah, I will pay the blood-money for this man you killed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, paid his blood-money."
"16491","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: When Amr ibn Sa'id sent to Mecca his expedition raiding Ibn al-Zubayr, Abu Shurayh came to him and spoke to him and informed him of what he heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he went out to the club of his people and sat in it, so I stood to him and sat with him, and he narrated to his people as he narrated to Amr ibn Sa'id what he heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and what Amr ibn Sa'id said to him. He said: I said this: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he conquered Mecca. Then on the morning after the conquest, Khuza'a attacked a man of Hudhayl and killed him while he was a polytheist. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us as an orator and said: O people, Allah, Exalted and Majestic, made Mecca sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah, Exalted, until the Day of Resurrection. It is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it nor to cut a tree in it. It was not lawful to anyone before me, nor is it lawful to anyone after me, and it was not lawful to me except this hour, out of anger at its people. Lo, it has returned as its sanctity yesterday. Lo, let the witness of you convey to the absent. Whoever says to you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fought in it, then say: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, made it lawful to His Messenger and did not make it lawful to you. O company of Khuza'a, lift your hands from killing, for much has occurred. If you kill a slain, I will pay it. Whoever is killed after this station of mine, his family have the better of two views: if they wish, the blood of his killer, and if they wish, his blood-money. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, paid the blood-money of the man Khuza'a killed. So Amr ibn Sa'id said to Abu Shurayh: Go away, O old man, for we know its sanctity better than you. It does not prevent a shedder of blood, nor one casting off obedience, nor one withholding jizya. He said: So I said: I was a witness and you were absent, and I have conveyed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us that our witness convey to our absent, and I have conveyed to you, so you and your affair."
"16492","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, and most of my knowledge is that my father narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the most insolent of people against Allah, Exalted and Majestic, is one who kills other than his killer, or seeks by the blood of the Jahiliyya from the people of Islam, or makes his eyes see in sleep what they did not see."
